## Remaining hits to note

The scan pattern cannot match a bare `resource-map.md`, so I ran a wider pass. Nothing live in the five verified paths. Five things sit outside the files this brief names:

1. `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/template-composition-system.md:31` still lists `resource-map.md` as a lazy support document rendered from template source. This is the closest live leftover: it is the same wrong claim the brief removed elsewhere, and it is in the feature-catalog.
2. `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/lib/frontmatter-migration.ts:139` maps `['resource-map.md', 'addons/resource-map.md.tmpl']`, and that template is now gone.
3. Generated data still lists the two deleted files: `runtime/data/trigger-index.json:2330`, `runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/corpus-manifest.json:7918` and `:7981`, `runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/generation-diagnostics.json:33802`. These need their own generator run, which the brief did not name.
4. `README.md:263` still says "Eighteen templates ship". It was already stale before this change (16 `.tmpl` files exist on disk) and is now further off (13 are enumerated in that section). I left it because no defensible number follows from the brief's edits.
5. Intentional keeps, as instructed: `README.md:258`, `SKILL.md:65` and `.hermes/.../SKILL.md:70` (deep-loop output), `SKILL.md:528` and `.hermes/.../SKILL.md:533` (ToC headings).

Nothing here needs an operator action to make the two verification commands pass. Items 1 through 4 need a scope decision, since each is a file or generated artifact this brief did not open.
